{"qid":"Q722071","names":["Ashanti Empire"],"title":"Ashanti Empire","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Ashanti (Asante) Empire was a Akan state centered on Kumasi in present-day Ghana, founded after Osei Tutu I defeated the Denkyira at the Battle of Feyiase in 1701 and united the Ashanti clans under the sacred Golden Stool. At its nineteenth-century peak the empire controlled most of modern Ghana plus parts of Côte d'Ivoire and Togo, with a population of three to four million and an elaborate bureaucracy financed by gold-trade revenues and Atlantic commerce. Five Anglo-Ashanti Wars between 1823 and 1900 progressively eroded Ashanti power; after the final conflict of 1900, Britain exiled Asantehene Agyeman Prempeh I to the Seychelles and formally annexed the territory to the Gold Coast Colony on 1 January 1902.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Core territorial extent is moderately well attested through British colonial surveys and oral tradition, though interior boundaries before c. 1820 remain approximate.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Ashanti Empire","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Ashanti-empire"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Ashanti Empire","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashanti_Empire"},{"label":"Britannica: Anglo-Ashanti Wars","url":"https://www.britannica.com/event/Anglo-Ashanti-Wars"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Ashanti Empire","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Osei Tutu I","nativeName":"Ɔsɛɛ Tutu I","roman":"Osei Tutu I","start":1701,"end":1717,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Opoku Ware I","nativeName":"Opoku Ware I","roman